@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Read the Sprints tab, a plan header, available stories, and members
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SprintsPage / SprintListView\nSprintPlanningPage / SprintPlanView" as page
  participant "ISprintService / SprintService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "SprintsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ListSprintsQueryHandler\nGetSprintPlanQueryHandler\nGetSprintCandidatesQueryHandler\nGetSprintMembersQueryHandler" as handler
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Open the Sprints tab, or a sprint's planning page
page -> client : Sprints tab: sprint list resource (ListSprintsQuery: plannedPage, closedPage, pageSize)\nPlanning page: workspace resource (IWorkspaceService.workspaceResource, GetWorkspaceQuery) for the\nbreadcrumb and project name; plan header (GetSprintPlanQuery), candidate (search, eligibleOnly false, page)\nand member (page) resources - independent caller-owned signal resources
client -> access : GET .../sprints, .../sprints/{sprintId}/plan, .../candidates, .../members
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once; sign in with this route as return route
else Authenticated (profile P: every active role reads sprints)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send the typed query through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-045 page 1 or more; page size 1-100, default 25
  alt Invalid page or page size
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : That list shows the page-size message without Try again or reference ID\n(the views always send page size 25, so only direct API callers meet this)
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle the query
    handler -> db : Read workspace mode and the sprint
    db --> handler : Mode and sprint, or none
    alt Workspace not found (the planning page's workspace read also answers 404)
      handler --> ctrl : 404
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : Project not found with Back to projects (planning page: project-not-found; Sprints tab:\nSprintListView emits notFound and SprintsPage calls the layout's refresh() on the first one)
    else Sprint not found (or in another workspace)
      handler --> ctrl : 404
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : Sprint not found state with Back to sprints (not-found)
    else Found
      handler -> db : One statement per list: bounded page plus total (window count),\nbacklog priority then story ID; rows omit descriptions
      db --> handler : Sprints tab: active sprint, one page of planned sprints by start date then ID,\none page of closed sprints newest closure first then ID, each with its total; or the plan header; or a candidate page with availability per row\n(eligible first, then Done or in another open sprint); or a member page, Done members included
      handler --> ctrl : Typed result with page, page size and total
      ctrl --> client : 200
      client --> page : Each resource updates its own value signal; pending marks apply by story ID;\nno sprints shows Plan your first sprint; Kanban mode shows plans read-only (paused);\na header that reads Active or Closed shows not-planned instead of the lists
      page --> actor : Present the header, available stories with reasons, and sprint members
    end
  end
end
opt Planning page opened with ?add={storyId} or ?remove={storyId}
  page -> page : A value that is not a well-formed story ID is ignored; nothing is marked
  page -> client : add: one candidate read with storyId (eligibleOnly false);\nremove: one member read with storyId
  client --> page : add: eligible joins toAdd and lists first under the sprint (paged state: HCK-130);\notherwise not marked and its row shows the reason. remove: returned as a current member joins\ntoRemove (paged state: HCK-126); otherwise nothing is marked
end
loop Search typing, or a page change in either list
  actor -> page : Type in search, or choose a page
  page -> client : Search debounces about 250 ms on the query signal and restarts at page 1;\npage actions are immediate; the resource aborts the superseded read
  client --> page : New page of that list only; the other list, the header and both pending sets are unchanged
end
opt Try again after a failed read
  actor -> page : Choose Try again
  page -> page : The view emits retryRequested: SprintsPage calls ProjectLayoutPage.refresh(), so the header and\nthe list reread together; SprintPlanningPage reloads its workspace resource and increments its counter
end
opt A committed dialog outcome, or a layout revision on the Sprints tab
  page -> page : The page increments its counter; the refresh input change rereads the list,\nor the plan header and both lists, keeping pages and both pending sets
end
note over ctrl, db
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043);
the page shows Load failed with the reference ID and Try again (error state).
A read that gets no response shows the same state with Try again and no reference ID.
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
